          "path": "_m/g/c/k/z/presaddfed-burial-chamber-wp/the-presaddfed-burial-chambers.jpg",
          "filename": "The Presaddfed Burial Chambers - geograph.org.uk - 986673.jpg",
          "caption": "The Presaddfed Burial Chambers. Dating from the 4th millennium BCE, the tomb, consisting of a pair of chambers once unified by a now diasppeared single cairn. is unusually sited at the bottom of a valley close to the upper end of Llyn Llywenan lake. The northern chamber has collapsed. The southern chamber, seen here to the right of the cows, was reputedly lived in for some time by an evicted farmer and his family in the early 19thC. Canny Anglesey folk were not averse to recycling ancient monuments \n see  849372",
          "alt": "The Presaddfed Burial Chambers. Dating from the 4th millennium BCE, the tomb, consisting of a pair of chambers once unified by a now diasppeared single cairn. is unusually sited at the bottom of a valley close to the upper end of Llyn Llywenan lake. The northern chamber has collapsed. The southern chamber, seen here to the right of the cows, was reputedly lived in for some time by an evicted farmer and his family in the early 19thC. Canny Anglesey folk were not averse to recycling ancient monuments \n see  849372",
          "width": 640,
